  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4100766a-e5f2-5ee0-a202-1b6b9eece34c" activityNameId="9c608ba9-a14e-5f7a-b46d-f5eea9e55595" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ammonia, partial oxidation, liquid, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ammonia, partial oxidation, liquid, at plant
Maunfacturing process starting with heavy fuel oil, air and electricity is considered, plus auxiliaries, energy, transportation, infrastructure and land use, as well as wastes and emissions into air and water. Transport of the raw materials, auxiliaries and wastes is included, transport and storage of the product are not included. Carbon Dioxide is the byproduct generated. Transcient or unstable operations are not considered, but the production during stable operation conditions. Emissions to air are considered as emanating in a high population density area. Emissions into water are assumed to be emitted into rivers. Values are taken principally from EFMA 2000 and Frischknecht 1999 (see report). Inventory refers to 1 kg 100% ammonia, at plant.;
CAS number: 007664-41-7; 
Formula: NH3; 
UUID: 64543a9c-8b3d-3397-9020-e4ab0028b9dd
&lt;null&gt;
Location: European average values
Technology: mostly present state of the art technology used in european ammonia production plants
Time period: Values based on reports from 1995 and 2000, and on literature with data from unknown date.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Sampling procedure: see OtherPeriodText 
Extrapolations: Transports based on standard distances of Ecoinvent. Infrastructure: proxy module used (chemical plant, organics)
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_64543a9c-8b3d-3397-9020-e4ab0028b9dd.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
